{#- post128: the DDL test cases (codegen.emit.ddl_tests) - read-only SQL and
    comments, one case per block; every value is filled in by the emitter from
    the resolved feed and the DDL the same run wrote. The environment trims
    block tags (trim_blocks / lstrip_blocks), so each tag sits on its own line. #}
-- DDL TEST CASES for {{ ddl_name | comment1 }} (feed {{ feed | comment1 }})
-- Run by the engineer AFTER the DDL, in a Databricks SQL editor or notebook. Read-only:
-- every statement is a SELECT or a SHOW. The agent writes these cases; it never runs them.
{% for key, value in banner %}
-- {{ key | comment1 }}: {{ value | comment1 }}
{% endfor %}
-- Each case says what it checks, the negative variant, and where its values come from,
-- then its SQL, if it has any.
-- Every SELECT checks itself: it returns one row (test_id, result, found, expected).
--   result PASS = as expected; FAIL = not as expected (compare found with expected);
{% if table_source %}
--   NO DATA = the table has no rows yet (run a test load first).
-- SHOW statements are checked by eye against their Expected lines. A case with no SQL
-- is a load test: run it with a test load from the source table through the framework.
{% else %}
--   NO DATA = the table has no rows yet (load a test file first).
-- SHOW statements are checked by eye against their Expected lines. A case with no SQL
-- is a load test: run it with a test file through the framework.
{% endif %}
{% for case in cases %}

-- {{ case.id }} {{ case.title }}
{% for line in case.lines %}
--   {{ line }}
{% endfor %}
{% for q in case.sql %}
{{ q.statement }};
{% for line in q.expected %}
--   {{ "Expected: " if loop.first else "          " }}{{ line }}
{% endfor %}
{% endfor %}
{% endfor %}
